{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RZrLBNZqf6j1WYGZByN8EZ","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have a comprehensive understanding. Let me compile my findings:\n\n## Full Experiment Plan & Median Tier Definition Report\n\n### File Locations Found\n\n**Main Experiment Plan Files:**\n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_10/projects/provenance_weight_training/experiment_plan.yaml` (272 lines)\n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_10/projects/solver-trace-ablation/experiment_plan.yaml`\n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_10/projects/pgpf-collapse-filter/experiment_plan.yaml`\n\n**Paper Framing Files (show project evolution):**\n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_10/projects/provenance_weight_training/paper_framing.md` (Main — Updated 2026-05-15 09:15 UTC)\n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_10/projects/provenance_weight_training/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260515T011902/best/paper_framing.md` (Path A scenario)\n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_10/projects/provenance_weight_training/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260515T011902/median/paper_framing.md` (Path B scenario — CURRENT DEFAULT)\n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_10/projects/provenance_weight_training/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260515T011902/worst/paper_framing.md` (Pivot scenario)\n\n**Dream Report Tier Definitions:**\n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_10/projects/provenance_weight_training/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260515T011902/meta.yaml` (3619 lines — master definition)\n\n**Registry & Supporting Files:**\n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_10/projects/provenance_weight_training/registry.yaml` (experiment metadata)\n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_10/projects/provenance_weight_training/dream_registry.yaml`\n\n**Imagined Experiments & Review Context:**\n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_10/projects/provenance_weight_training/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260515T011902/median/imagined_experiments.yaml`\n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_10/projects/provenance_weight_training/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260515T011902/median/review_context.yaml`\n\n---\n\n### Experiment Plan Structure (provenance_weight_training)\n\nThe main experiment plan contains **27 experiments** organized in priority tiers:\n\n**MVP Phase (PRIORITY MVP)** — 6 experiments: uniform baselines, grid-b sweeps (b=0.5/1.0/1.5/2.0/3.0/5.0), adaptive_fix validation\n\n**P0 Phase** — 13 experiments: grid-b low (b<0.5), contamination 60% datasets, n_min ablation (1-5), tau sweeps, batch_size effects, ESS-only baseline, Golden Ratio baseline, batchsize variations\n\n**P1 Phase** — 6 experiments: ModernBERT detector, cross-generator training, Llama-3.2-3B setup, baselines (detect-and-remove, random reweighting)\n\n**P2 Phase** — 2 experiments: domain-skewed injection, downstream evaluation (MMLU/HellaSwag)\n\n**Key Constraints:** 4x RTX 6000 Pro 96G GPUs, ~180 hours total budget, MVP ~85h, Remaining ~95h. Target venue: EMNLP 2026 ARR May 25.\n\n---\n\n### Core Research Framing\n\n**Main Claim Structure (3 Claims):**\n1. **Claim 1 (Primary)**: Dual-constrained adaptive b* (α_eff + ESS bounds) provides principled weight exponent derivation vs. Drayson's per-model empirical grid search\n2. **Claim 2 (Primary)**: Adaptive b* matches grid-best within seed variance at zero tuning cost (6N → 1 runs)\n3. **Claim 3 (Setting)**: Method works without knowing contamination proportion—only needs detector scores, no validation set\n\n**Method Core:**\n- α_eff(b) ≥ τ — quality lower bound (\"ensure enough clean data\")\n- ESS(b) ≥ n_min — stability upper bound (\"don't downweight too aggressively\")\n- b* = inf{b ≥ 0 : α_eff(b) ≥ τ} — minimum intervention principle\n- Implementation: direct loss reweighting (not SIR resampling like Drayson)\n\n---\n\n### MEDIAN TIER DEFINITION (Key Finding)\n\nThe **median tier** is defined in `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_10/projects/provenance_weight_training/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260515T011902/meta.yaml` (lines 49-85). Here's the complete definition:\n\n```yaml\nmedian:\n  tier: median\n  meaning: >\n    Adaptive b* 稳定工作但效应放大有限，维持 Path B 叙事——within variance + zero cost\n    (Adaptive b* works stably but effect amplification is limited. Maintain Path B narrative—\n    within seed variance + zero computational cost)\n  \n  key_assumptions:\n    - b=0.5 处于或接近真最优，finer grid 可能在 b=0.3 略优但差异 <0.005 PPL\n      (b=0.5 is at or near true optimum; finer grid might be slightly better at b=0.3 \n       but difference < 0.005 PPL)\n    \n    - 60%/3B 效应放大温和（1.5-3x），不足以单独作为 selling point\n      (60% contamination/3B model effect amplification is moderate (1.5-3x), \n       insufficient as standalone selling point)\n    \n    - Adaptive b* median 系统性高于 grid-best b（~0.8 vs ~0.5），但 PPL landscape 足够平坦使差异不显著\n      (Adaptive b* median systematically higher than grid-best b (~0.8 vs ~0.5), \n       but PPL landscape flat enough that difference is not significant)\n    \n    - 少数设置（domain-skewed, certain generators）adaptive 表现较弱，aggregate ratio 被拉低\n      (Few settings show weaker adaptive performance, pulling down aggregate ratio)\n    \n    - 下游任务改善不一致：部分 task 可测，部分在噪声范围内\n      (Downstream task improvements inconsistent: some measurable, some within noise)\n  \n  number_ranges:\n    aggregate_ratio_pct: [80, 95]  # Adaptive PPL as % of grid-best improvement\n    max_relative_ppl_improvement_pct: [0.4, 0.8]\n    cross_setting_win_rate: [0.75, 0.9]\n    adaptive_within_seed_var_of_gridbest_fraction: [0.6, 0.85]\n    downstream_mmlu_delta_abs_pct: [0.0, 0.3]\n    finer_grid_best_b: [0.2, 0.5]  # True optimum b in finer grid is in this range\n  \n  narrative_direction: >\n    维持 Path B: \"adaptive matches grid-best within seed variance, \n    eliminating grid search (6N→1)\"。需补充实验强化叙事：\n    (a) n_min sensitivity curve 展示单超参鲁棒性，\n    (b) 计算成本对比表（grid search GPU-hours vs adaptive 零额外成本），\n    (c) 对表现较弱的设置做 per-batch b* 分布诊断，解释为何 aggregate ratio <95%。\n    Claim 2 措辞保守化为 \"comparable performance at zero tuning cost\"， \n    避免用 \"match\" 暗示数值相等。\n    \n    (Maintain Path B: \"adaptive matches grid-best within seed variance, \n    eliminating grid search (6N→1)\". Need supporting experiments:\n    (a) n_min sensitivity curve showing single-hyperparameter robustness,\n    (b) cost-comparison table (grid search GPU-hours vs adaptive zero overhead),\n    (c) per-batch b* distribution diagnosis for weaker settings, explaining \n        why aggregate ratio <95%.\n    Rephrase Claim 2 conservatively as \"comparable performance at zero tuning cost\",\n    avoid \"match\" suggesting numerical equivalence.)\n```\n\n---\n\n### Median Tier: Imagined Experiments Specification\n\nThe **median scenario** includes concrete **imagined experiments** with expected numerical results:\n\n**Grid-b low (b=0.1/0.2/0.3) experiments**, 3 seeds:\n- Seed42: b=0.1 → 17.662 PPL, b=0.3 → 17.648 PPL (best in extended grid), b=0.5 → 17.651\n- Seed123: b=0.3 → 17.636 (vs b=0.5 → 17.638, diff 0.002)\n- Seed456: b=0.3 → 17.649 (vs b=0.5 → 17.650, diff 0.001)\n\n**Key finding for median tier:** PPL landscape is extremely flat (b=0.1-0.5 range spans only 0.014 PPL total). Adaptive b* median (~0.88) is systematically higher than grid-best b (~0.3-0.5), but this doesn't cause significant PPL loss because the landscape is so flat. This justifies the \"within seed variance\" framing.\n\n---\n\n### Critical Distinctions Between Tiers (Best/Median/Worst)\n\n**BEST TIER** (aggregate_ratio 95-115%):\n- Finer grid confirms b=0.5 is true optimum or in broad [0.3, 0.5] minimum plateau\n- 60%/3B settings show 3-5x effect amplification\n- Claim 2 upgraded to \"matches or exceeds grid-best\"\n- Narrative: \"Adaptive is not just free but also effective\"\n\n**MEDIAN TIER** (aggregate_ratio 80-95%):\n- Finer grid shows b=0.3 slightly better than b=0.5, but difference <0.005 PPL\n- 60%/3B shows only 1.5-3x amplification\n- Path B preserved (conservative framing)\n- Narrative: \"Adaptive is comparable to grid-best, and free\"\n- **Currently expected most likely scenario based on MVP results (88.6% ratio)**\n\n**WORST TIER** (aggregate_ratio 55-80%):\n- True optimum b lies outside original grid (b=0.1-0.3), adaptive overshoot to ~0.87 is problematic\n- No meaningful effect amplification at higher contamination/model size\n- Claims require major reframing\n- Pivot strategy: reposition α_eff(b) as diagnostic framework rather than optimization method\n\n---\n\n### Summary of Key Context\n\nThe **median tier definition** encodes expected outcomes if:\n1. Extended grid search reveals b≈0.3 is marginally better than b=0.5, but within seed noise\n2. PPL landscape is very flat (b selection doesn't matter much)\n3. Effect amplification at 60%/3B is modest (1.5-3x, not 3-5x)\n4. Adaptive b* systematically overestimates (median ~0.88 vs optimal ~0.3-0.5) but landscape's flatness cushions this\n\nThis is the **default Path B** framing used to address concerns about small effect size (~0.3% PPL) and to maintain publication viability even if results are not as strong as hoped."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c2699f91-58b1-43cd-84dd-ccef8205b378","uuid":"bd8ce973-7263-42a4-9ec5-61b77cbcf5e0","timestamp":"2026-05-15T10:33:16.395Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In the directory /home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_10, find and read:\n1. Any YAML files related to experiment plans or registry\n2. Any files named paper_framing.md or experiment_plan*\n3. Any files with \"tier\" or \"median\" in the name\n\nI need to understand the full experiment plan structure and any additional context about the median tier definition. Report file paths and key contents. Be thorough.","agentId":"abe9f16dc47b6952a","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"tex